---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figures from '../components/Figures.astro';
import Invite from '../components/Invite.astro';
import { aboutFigures } from '../data/proof';
---
<Base title="About" description="Karol Piątek, Staff iOS Engineer and AI Champion at TransferGo: what he has built to make AI useful on a real team, with the numbers.">
  <section class="page-head" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h1 id="about-title">What I’ve built to make AI useful on a real team.</h1>
    <p class="page-head__lede">
      I’m a Staff iOS Engineer and the AI Champion at TransferGo. The numbers come first, the longer story follows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Figures items={aboutFigures} cols={3} />

  <div class="about-body">
    <h2 id="currently">Currently</h2>
    <p><strong>Staff iOS Engineer, TransferGo</strong>, Platform team (Apr 2025 to present)</p>
    <ul>
      <li>AI Champion for the company; the iOS guild reached <strong>100% daily AI usage</strong></li>
      <li>Introduced the team’s AI building blocks: <strong>17 custom skills</strong>, rules and commands now part of the daily workflow</li>
      <li>Built a background agent that ships small, reviewable PRs to align the codebase for AI</li>
      <li>Built a weekly workflow that mines code review comments and turns recurring ones into lint rules and skill updates</li>
      <li>Moved <strong>about 40% of manual regression work</strong> to the agent with an AI workflow and UI tests built into the SDLC</li>
      <li>Deliver whole features across all platforms and mentor engineers</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Selected outcomes</h2>

    <div class="outcome-group">
      <h3>Engineering velocity and quality</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Took test coverage from <strong>5% to 50% in a year</strong> on a complex production app at Netguru</li>
        <li>Cut clean-build time by <strong>40 seconds</strong> at TransferGo, which compounds across every developer, every day</li>
        <li>Automated most of the iOS release process at TransferGo</li>
        <li>Led the migration from <strong>Resolver to Factory</strong> for dependency injection at TransferGo, so dependency resolution is checked at compile time</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="outcome-group">
      <h3>Cross-functional leadership</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>DRI for TransferGo’s Receivers feature, aligning <strong>3 cross-functional teams</strong> on the technical side</li>
        <li>Led Netguru’s <strong>Mobile Security Group</strong> (2021-2022): built the <a href="https://github.com/netguru/mobile-security-checklist">mobile security checklist</a>, defined the security career path, ran a monthly “Let’s hack together” event</li>
        <li>Led Netguru’s iOS R&amp;D function and set the research agenda for the iOS practice</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="outcome-group">
      <h3>Architecture and migration</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Authored the SwiftUI migration playbook at smartpatient (MyTherapy app): modules, DI, formatting standards</li>
        <li>Led the SwiftUI refactor across multiple legacy features at TransferGo</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      Nearly a decade in iOS engineering. Staff at <strong>TransferGo</strong> today; before that, Senior at <strong>smartpatient</strong> (MyTherapy app), <strong>Netguru</strong> (fintech, banking and retail platforms, where I also led the Mobile Security Group), and earlier roles at <strong>Gigaset</strong> (smart-home IoT) and <strong>Human Device</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open-source contributor to <a href="https://github.com/OWASP/owasp-mstg">OWASP MSTG</a> and <a href="https://github.com/MobSF/Mobile-Security-Framework-MobSF">MobSF</a>, the reference projects for mobile app security.
    </p>

    <h2>How I think</h2>
    <p>Building with AI:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/ai-is-a-system">AI is a system, not a skill: why one piece never moves the needle</a></li>
      <li><a href="/ai-guardrails-pyramid">The guardrails pyramid: keeping AI-written iOS code in line</a></li>
      <li><a href="/migrate-codebase-with-ai">Migrate your codebase automatically with AI, 1% a day</a></li>
      <li><a href="/mine-review-comments-with-ai">Every review comment you repeat is a bug in your guardrails</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>From before the AI work:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/Initialization-side-effects">Initialization side effects</a></li>
      <li><a href="/How-to-save-milions-in-software-development-1">How to save millions in software development</a></li>
      <li><a href="/including-production-changes-for-unit-tests">Including production changes for unit tests</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <Invite />
</Base>
